  "note": "Poll on Wednesday 20 May 1964, in the 80 per cent region; results declared by Don Ryan, returning officer, between about 11.30 p.m. and 2.45 a.m. (Armagh Guardian, 21 May 1964). All five wards were contested. Labels as printed: C.R. and R.A. are the two ratepayers' groups (R.A., the Ratepayers' Association, whose chairman Norman Creswell topped the South-West poll; C.R. is not expanded in the source), N. Nationalist, U. Unionist. The new council: 12 Unionists, six Ratepayers, one Trade Unionist and one Nationalist."
